From 1349c4ad2c4268368c32da7fa903f790d06f3c62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Anderson <iana@apple.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Oct 2025 10:15:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/52] UPSTREAM: [clang][headers] Need a way for math.h to
 share the definitions of INIFINITY and NAN with float.h (#164348)

In C23 mode, both float.h and math.h are required to define INIFINITY
and NAN. However, with clang modules, there needs to be a single owner
for the declarations. Let that be float.h since that's the suggested
true owner in Annex F.2.2 of ISO/IEC 9899:2024, and introduce
`__need_infinity_nan` so that math.h can pick up the compiler
definitions.

(cherry picked from commit 38473c5d351d6b2ae21b5eb1ce66c2bcc2f7c6f7)
